    `let cur = s.m;` -- source is a STRUCT FIELD                clean
    `Vec[Vec[i64]]` element read out, `.len()`                  clean

So leg A needs, together: the source is a Vec ELEMENT (a binding or struct field is clean), the read goes into a `let` (inline indexing is clean), and the binding is consumed by `.get()` (`.len()` is clean). 602 B / 4 allocations is the whole Map control block plus buckets -- not a fragment.

