  KARAC_AUTO_PAR=0 build   : x dR dR end     <- WRONG

`r` is moved out of `h` by the pattern and dropped at the end of the arm -- exactly one `dR`. The compiled backends drop the moved-out binding AND still run the partially-moved `h`'s field cleanup, so the body fires a second time.

